{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/they-came-from/beyond-the-grave/1555882-first-impressions-of-beyond-the-grave","id":1555882,"title":"First Impressions of Beyond the Grave","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","They Came From...","...Beyond the Grave!"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-11-26T01:46:40-08:00","id":1555882,"title":"First Impressions of Beyond the Grave","content":"Hey guys,<br /> <br /> I've owned my copy of this book for some time but never got a chance to read it due to a bunch of issues popping up until this weekend. It's really something I should have checked out much earlier too because I'm a big fan of Hammer Horror and can identify about half of the movies that are being homaged throughout the story.<br /> <br /> I really like the variations based on decades as well as the metatextual ideas of treating this game as as an in-universe movie.<br /> <br /> I admit part of me thinks this would be the perfect gameline to do a Scooby Doo game (probably with R-rated horrifying murder because, of course and I'm an evil monster as an ST). You can easily stat out the Great Dane and teenagers on this logic.<br /> <br /> Favorite parts:<br /> <br /> * THE DEVIL HIMSELF<br /> * Dracula, of course<br /> * Dracula's brides<br /> * Frankenstein<br /> * The Slashers<br /> * The snotty vampire nobles<br /> * The feral vampires<br /> <br /> Okay, pretty much the entirety of the monster section that I do think was the highlight.<br /> <br /> I was also a big fan of the adventure with the witches as I admit, I would have made a differentiation between SEXY EVIL WITCHES and OLD CRONE WITCHES as monster types with the possibility of one turning into the other.<br /> <br /> What were your impressions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&am